/* __acad3dV62 (maintenance fix): the vendored third-party @font-face bundle that used to occupy
   this block was removed. It declared a single family whose every source was a remote CDN URL, so
   it could only load with a live internet connection -- a hard external dependency, directly
   against this project's own local-first principle ("the released app must work without a server
   or external dependency"). Offline it produced 25 failed network requests on every page load and
   silently fell back to the stacks already declared throughout this stylesheet, so removing it
   makes the offline rendering the only rendering rather than the accidental one. Its companion
   body-class rule went with it: that rule was BOTH universal (body.CLASS *) and !important, so it
   also overrode every deliberate element-level font choice in the file -- the hex colour field's
   monospace and the measurement labels' Consolas among them -- which now render as their own rules
   always intended. The base stack in the first <style> block (body{font:15px/1.5 -apple-system,...})
   plus each component's own font-family declarations carry the UI from here. */


