/* __acad3dV69: the 2D board's material cards, published for the BIM module. This is the FIRST
   model-level connection between the two engines in this file -- everything before it unified
   the shell only. Deliberately the SAME ARRAY, not a copy: two lists that start identical and
   drift are worse than one list, and 'one connected model' (Product Principle 3) means the
   BIM inspector and the board's Material Cards dialog cannot disagree about what Concrete is.
   Published on window because the two engines live in separate <script> blocks with no shared
   scope; the BIM side reads it through bimMaterialCards() and treats an absent library as
