/* __acad3dV70: the ribbon stands down in the BIM workspace, replaced by the floating tool
   dock (#a3d-dock) over the drawing -- the Rayon arrangement. The dock is GENERATED from
   A3DR_TABS, the same registry the ribbon renders from, so no command can be lost by this
   swap; that is asserted set-for-set by the Phase 70 suite rather than trusted.
   --acad-ribbon-h is the contract every other surface positions against (see the comment on
   the .acad-doctab rules). Its parts are 28 QAT + 26 tabs + 104 panels + 24 doctabs = 182;
   hiding the tab strip and the panel row leaves 28 + 24 = 52. The QAT keeps file/undo/redo
   and the workspace switcher, and the doc tabs keep document switching -- removing those
   would leave no way back out of this workspace. */
body.a3d-mode #acad-panels,
body.a3d-mode #acad-tabs{display:none!important}
body.a3d-mode{--acad-ribbon-h:52px}
